      "content": "9. Government of India Act 1858"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Lord Canning was the Governor-General of India during the Revolt of 1857 and became the first Viceroy of India after the GOI Act 1858.",
        "Mangal Pandey, attached to the 34th Bengal Native Infantry, fired at his officers in Barrackpore on March 29, 1857.",
        "The GOI Act 1858 abolished the Board of Control and Court of Directors, creating the office of the Secretary of State for India."
      ],
      "id": "m2zbscm"
